N Calculator for each combination of p and r.

Monte Carlo Uncertainty Calculator for each combination of p and N.

Tabulated Values Provider for each tabulated value.

Inverse Calculator for each combination of N and r, and N and p.

Warning Generator for each warning code.

Integration tests:

Compute N for p = 0.05 and r = 0.10. Verify N = 1900.

Compute N for p = 0.01 and r = 0.01. Verify N = 1000000.

Compute tabulated values for p = 0.05. Verify the tabulated values.

Compute from N for N = 10000 and r = 0.10. Verify p = 0.0099.

Compute from N for N = 10000 and p = 0.05. Verify r = 0.0436.

Worked-example tests:

Section 8 of the Null-Model Protocol paper: verify the tabulated values.

Section 11.1 of the Null-Model Protocol paper: N = 10^4 gives a standard error of about 5.5 * 10^-4 and a relative error of about 18 percent for p = 2.99 * 10^-3.

